// Title: Suspicious Service Installed
// Sigma ID: f2485272-a156-4773-82d7-1d178bc4905b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: xknow (@xknow_infosec), xorxes (@xor_xes)
// Date: 2019-04-08 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects installation of NalDrv or PROCEXP152 services via registry-keys to non-system32 folders.
//   Both services are used in the tool Ghost-In-The-Logs (https://github.com/bats3c/Ghost-In-The-
//   Logs), which uses KDU (https://github.com/hfiref0x/KDU)
// False positives:
//   - Other legimate tools using this service names and drivers. Note - clever attackers may easily bypass this detection by just renaming the services. Therefore just Medium-level and don't rely on it.
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20200419024230/https://blog.dylan.codes/evading-sysmon-and-windows-event-logging/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_susp_service_installed.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey in~ ("HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet001\\Services\\NalDrv\\ImagePath", "HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet001\\Services\\PROCEXP152\\ImagePath")) and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procexp64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procexp64a.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procexp.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procmon64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procmon64a.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procmon.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\handle.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\handle64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\handle64a.exe") and RegistryValueData contains "\\WINDOWS\\system32\\Drivers\\PROCEXP152.SYS")))
